# Credentials (ENG-765 / VM-05). This package is PUBLIC on npm and examples here take a
# real Vault API key to run, so a working .env is the natural thing to have sitting in a
# clone. The leading dot does not match `something.env.yaml` — both shapes are listed on
# purpose; that gap published a live Firebase Admin key out of igniteiq-platform.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.env.yaml
*.env.yml
*.key
*.pem
service-account*.json
*-key.json

# Agent session state and per-session worktrees. Worktrees live INSIDE the repo at
# .claude/worktrees/<name>, so without this a `git add -A` in the shared checkout tries to
# commit an embedded git repository (2026-08-27, 2026-08-31).
.claude/
